  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "hb_set_copy",
    "file": "harfbuzz/src/hb-set.cc",
    "description": "hb_set_copy() unconditionally dereferences the result of hb_set_create() and calls copy->set(*set) without checking allocation success. In the fuzz harness, alloc_state is set to input size; with this PoC the tiny input drives allocation failure paths, so hb_set_create() can return an invalid/null-like set object. copy->set then reaches hb_bit_set_invertible_t::set (harfbuzz/src/hb-bit-set-invertible.hh:129) and performs a write through an uninitialized/invalid internal bitset pointer, causing the wild write SEGV.",
    "conditions": "Data flow: LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput sets alloc_state=size, creates a face from attacker bytes, then trySubset()->hb_subset_or_fail()->hb_subset_plan_create(). During plan creation, hb_set_copy(input->sets.drop_tables) (and similar copies) is called. Trigger requires allocator-failure mode (induced here by very small input via failing-alloc logic) so hb_set_create inside hb_set_copy does not yield a valid initialized set; because hb_set_copy lacks an in_error/null check before copy->set(*set), it crashes in hb_bit_set_invertible_t::set."
  },
